## Directory Structure

- `build/` - Contains scripts for building Singularity images and virtual environments
  - `image.sh` - Script to build the Singularity image
  - `venv.sh` - Script to create and set up the virtual environment
- `execute/` - Contains execution scripts for different environments
  - `local/` - Scripts for local execution
  - `hpc/` - Scripts for HPC execution (SLURM, PBS, LSF)
- `install_requirements.sh` - Script to install dependencies
- `main.py` - Main execution script
- `${process_id}.def` - Singularity definition file

## Setup

Before executing the process, you need to either build the Singularity image or create the virtual environment.

### Building the Singularity Image

```bash
# Navigate to the build directory
cd build

# Run the image build script
./image.sh
```

The image will be built and stored at: ${image_path}

### Creating the Virtual Environment

```bash
# Navigate to the build directory
cd build

# Run the virtual environment build script
./venv.sh
```

The virtual environment will be created at: ${venv_path}

## Usage

This process can be executed either as a script (using a virtual environment) or as a container (using Singularity/Apptainer).

### Configuration

The execution scripts already contain all the necessary configuration. You just need to:

1. Set the required environment variables before running the scripts
2. Specify bind paths as environment variables (converted to either container bind mounts or symbolic links)

